      <main class="page-main" id="main-content">
<section class="hero" id="module">
  <p class="eyebrow">Lean module · Projected OGD</p>
  <h1 class="page-title identifier-title">Bandit<wbr>RL<wbr>Proof.<wbr>Online<wbr>Gradient<wbr>Descent</h1>
  <p class="lede">Orabona, arXiv:1912.13213v10, Algorithm 2.1, Proposition 2.11, Lemma 2.12, Theorem 2.13 (constant step only), and Eq. (2.1). Time t = 0 denotes source round 1; iterate ... T is source x_(T+1). The Hilbert-space interfaces specialize to finite-dimensional real Euclidean spaces. Loss-dependent declarations below use the stronger historical RegularLoss predicate. OnlineGradientDescentSource supplies the arbitrary-open source regularity interface on the same algorithms. Projection and causal feasibility statements need no loss regularity.</p>
</section>

