<details class="declaration" id="decl-ae1e99dac73d">
  <summary>
    <span class="kind">theorem</span>
    <code>BanditRL.OnlineGradientDescent.project_existsUnique</code>
    <span><span class="status compiled">Compiled</span> </span>
  </summary>
  <div class="declaration-content">
    <p class="docstring">Every nonempty closed convex domain has a unique nearest point before any choice is made.
This establishes the well-definedness of the same projection used below.</p>
    <div class="node-memberships"><p><strong>Used in these reading views:</strong> <a href="../../books/online-learning/index.html">Online Learning Book</a></p>
<p><a href="../../chapters/online-ogd/index.html">Projected OGD: Orabona Chapter 2</a></p>
<details><summary>Canonical node identity</summary><code>declaration:BanditRL.OnlineGradientDescent.project_existsUnique</code><p>Reading membership is not a proof dependency. Exact assumptions remain in the Lean statement.</p></details></div>
    <pre class="lean-code"><code><span class="kw">theorem</span> project_existsUnique (V : Domain E) (z : E) : ∃! p : E, p ∈ V.carrier ∧ ‖z - p‖ = ⨅ w : V.carrier, ‖z - w‖</code></pre>
